L236: Aims:
L237: Our aim is to implement two studies; the first will measure the effect that d-aspartic acid
L238: supplementation has on basal testosterone levels in advanced trainers, whilst they are
L239: undergoing standardised training. The second study will explore effects of d-aspartic acid
L240: supplementation on strength, hypertrophy and neural adaptation with concurrent resistance
L241: training over a period of 6 months.
L242: Primary Objectives
L243: Study 1
L244: - To measure change in basal testosterone levels from three different doses of DAA (0g, 3g,
L245: 6g).
L246: - To examine the effect of the recommended (3g) dose compared to a double-dose (6g)
L247: protocol.
L248: Study 2
L249: - To determine the relationship between d-aspartic acid and strength after 24 weeks of
L250: resistance training
L251: - To determine the relationship between testosterone change and neural adaptation after 24
L252: weeks of resistance training
L253: - To determine the relationship between testosterone change and hypertrophy after 24 weeks
L254: of resistance training
L255: Proposal research design:
L256: The first study (acute) will be a double blinded randomised controlled trial that will explore two
L257: dosing strategies of DAA. The cohort will comprise of men experienced in resistance training
L258: who are currently training. This study will be conducted over 4-weeks, with an initial 2-week
L259: Commercial-in-Confidence
L260: standardisation period.At the end of the two week standardisation period baseline blood draws
L261: will be taken. Then participants will be allocated to one of three groups D6, D3, D0 which will
L262: be 6 grams, 3 grams and 0 grams of DAA respectively. Participants will consume their relevant
L263: dose daily for 12 days
L264: The second study will be a double blinded randomised controlled trial that will compare the
L265: outcomes of the participants assigned to the experimental treatment groups with those
L266: assigned to the placebo control group. The cohort will comprise of healthy participants
L267: experienced in resistance training. Participants will be randomised to their group, either 3g
