L275: ## **Administrative Section**
L276: ### **1. TITLE AND SUMMARY OF PROJECT**
L277: **1.1. Title**
L278: **1.1.1 What is the formal title of this research proposal?**
L279: The effect of D-Aspartic Acid on adaptation from a 24 week resistance training program
L280: **1.1.2 What is the short title / acronym of this research proposal (if applicable)?**
L281: Effects of DAA during resistance training
L282: **1.2. Description of the project in plain language**
L283: **1.2.1 Give a concise and simple description (not more than 400 words), in plain language, of the aims of this**
L284: **project, the proposal research design and the methods to be used to achieve those aims.**
L285: Aims:
L286: Our aim is to implement two studies; the first will measure the effect that d-aspartic acid supplementation
L287: has on basal testosterone levels in advanced trainers, whilst they are undergoing standardised training. The
L288: second study will explore effects of d-aspartic acid supplementation on strength, hypertrophy and neural
L289: adaptation with concurrent resistance training over a period of 6 months.
L290: Primary Objectives
L291: Study 1
L292:       - To measure change in basal testosterone levels from three different doses of DAA (0g, 3g, 6g).
L293:       - To examine the effect of the recommended (3g) dose compared to a double-dose (6g) protocol.
L294: Study 2
L295:        - To determine the relationship between d-aspartic acid and strength after 24 weeks of resistance training
L296:       - To determine the relationship between testosterone change and neural adaptation after 24 weeks of
L297: resistance training
L298:       - To determine the relationship between testosterone change and hypertrophy after 24 weeks of resistance
L299: training
L300: Proposal research design:
L301: The first study (acute) will be a double blinded randomised controlled trial that will explore two dosing
L302: strategies of DAA. The cohort will comprise of men experienced in resistance training who are currently
L303: training. This study will be conducted over 4-weeks, with an initial 2-week standardisation period.At the end
L304: of the two week standardisation period baseline blood draws will be taken. Then participants will be
L305: allocated to one of three groups D6, D3, D0 which will be 6 grams, 3 grams and 0 grams of DAA
L306: respectively. Participants will consume their relevant dose daily for 12 days
L307: The second study will be a double blinded randomised controlled trial that will compare the outcomes of the
L308: participants assigned to the experimental treatment groups with those assigned to the placebo control group.
L309: The cohort will comprise of healthy participants experienced in resistance training. Participants will be
L310: randomised to their group, either 3g D-Asp (D3), 6g D-Asp (D6) or placebo (P) then begin their daily
L311: allocated dose and resistance training program for 12 weeks. After training for 12 weeks both groups will
L312: have a one week break (de-load week) to help prevent overtraining. They will then continue training for
L313: another 12 weeks. 5 blood draws will be taken in total. These will be conducted at baseline, 12 days, 30
L314: days, 90 days and 180 days.
