L852: If the source of the contamination is known, arrangements should be made to collect a blood sample from
L853: the source by the team looking after that source subject, (preferably not the injured staff member), after they
L854: have given informed written consent.
L855: Inform the Occupational Health service immediately of the incident, so that a risk assessment can be
L856: undertaken and if necessary post-exposure prophylaxis can begin within 1 hour or as soon as possible. If
L857: the inoculation occurs outside of normal working hours, attend Accident and Emergency Department for a
L858: further risk assessment.
