L999: **6.3. Participation experience**
L1000: **6.3.1 Provide a concise detailed description, in not more than 200 words, in terms which are easily**
L1001: **understood by the lay reader of what the participation will involve.**
L1002: Study 1 will involve 2 weeks standardised training before the experimental period begins. Baseline testing
L1003: will commence at the end of week 2 (involving 1 repetition max testing and a venous blood-draw).
L1004: Participants will be randomised to one of three groups and begin their daily allocated dose (0g 3g or 6g) and
L1005: continue training for a further 12 days. After 12 days a post blood draw will be taken along with strength
L1006: testing.
L1007: Study 2 will involve 12 laboratory testing sessions, where strength (1RM, neural adaptation (electrical nerve
L1008: stimulation), hypertrophy (ultrasound) and testosterone (venous blood) will be measured. For the duration of
L1009: the study participants will be consuming capsules daily either containing placebo or a testosterone boosting
L1010: supplement. They will also be attending the University of Western Sydney research gym four times per week
L1011: for the 6 month duration of the study. Post workout nutrition will be provided in liquid form at the end of each
L1012: session.
L1013: For more information please refer to attached participation information sheet –study 1 and participation
L1014: information sheet study 2.
