L1066: **6.5.3... Do you intend to include both males and females in this study?** No
L1067: **6.5.3... Please explain why only one sex is involved in the study.** **In doing this you will need to demonstrate**
L1068: **why this approach is valid.**
L1069: The main outcome measure for the proposed study is testosterone levels. The supplement d-aspartic acid is
L1070: known to increase testosterone levels by accumulating in the testes and up-regulating transportation of
L1071: cholesterol which is a limiting factor in the rate of testosterone production. Currently there has been no
L1072: research conducted on the effects of d-aspartic acid on testosterone levels in women.
