L1082: The effect of a testosterone boosting supplement on adaptation from a 24 week resistance training
L1083: program?
L1084: Please find below/attached an information document detailing your role as a potential participant in this
L1085: project. You may register your interest in participating in this research project with myself (Geoff Melville –
L1086: Principle Researcher) where you will be forwarded a participant information sheet for you to decide if you
L1087: wish to participate in this research. Testing is expected to be underway in April 2013.
L1088: Participants involved in this project will undergo 2 weeks of standardised training. Baseline testing will
L1089: commence at the end of this week. Participants will be randomised to their group, either 3g Supplement(S3),
L1090: 6g Supp (S6) or placebo (S0) then begin their daily allocated dose and resistance training program for 12
L1091: weeks. After training for 12 weeks both groups will have a one week break (de-load week) to help prevent
L1092: overtraining, during this period groups will also stop taking d-asp/placebo pills, they will then continue
L1093: training for another 12 weeks and start taking the d-asp/placebo again. Eight blood draws will be taken in
L1094: total. These will be conducted at baseline, 12 days, 30 days, 90 days, second baseline and repeated
L1095: measures at the same time points will follow for the next 12w cycle.
L1096: Phase two will involve 2 groups, S0 and experimental group S. Participants will conduct 12 weeks of
L1097: training, a one week break, then another 12 weeks of training, with the experimental group consuming DAA
L1098: daily for the whole 25 weeks. Strength and neural testing will be conducted pre, mid and post training.
L1099: I would like to thank you for considering this invitation.
L1100: Kind regards,
L1101: Geoff Melville (AEP)
L1102: PhD Candidate, Exercise Science
