L1199: Relevant medical history (pre exercise health screening questionnaire).
L1200: Strength levels during a squat and bench press exercise
L1201: Size of the quadriceps muscles (thigh) using non-invasive doppler ultrasound imaging techniques.
L1202: Muscle activation of the quadriceps muscles using surface electromyography.
L1203: Neural adaptation to resistance training via changes in evoked v-wave and h-reflex responses.
L1204: Changes in testosterone will be measured via a venipuncture collection of a blood sample taken in the
L1205: morning after a 12h fast. Fingerprick samples of blood will also be collected for the measurement of HDL
L1206: cholesterol.
